{# Stands in for `_layouts/basecp.twig` when a Twig-rendered control panel
   screen is to render inside the Inertia shell rather than as its own
   document.

   `_layouts/cp.twig` captures its fragments before handing control to its
   parent — it has to, to assemble the document — so by the time this runs they
   are already strings in the context. All this does is pass them along and
   draw nothing: the response layer picks them up and renders the shell around
   them.

   The names match what `CpScreenResponseFormatter` sends for an `asCpScreen()`
   screen, so `cp/Screen` can't tell the two apart.

   Extends nothing on purpose. `basecp` → `base` is where `<html>` is written,
   and the point here is that no document gets built.

   @see CraftCms\Cms\View\LegacyScreenFragments
#}

{# `bodyClass` was applied to the document's own `<body>`, and plugin CSS leans
   on it — Commerce scopes its order index to `.commerceorders`. The shell owns
   `<body>`, so the classes travel as a prop and the screen applies them for as
   long as it is on screen. `bodyAttributes` does not come along: the shell
   manages those itself. #}

{# The document puts the footer inside the content column, right below the
   content itself — `_elements/footer` pagination, usually. The shell has no
   slot of its own for it, so it travels with the content it sat under. #}
{%- set footerHtml = footer
    ? "<div id=\"footer\" class=\"flex flex-justify\">#{footer}</div>"
    : '' -%}

{%- do craft.cp.collectScreenFragments({
    docTitle: docTitle ?? null,
    title: title ?? null,
    selectedSubnavItem: selectedSubnavItem ?? null,
    crumbs: crumbs,
    contextMenu: contextMenu,
    toolbar: toolbar,
    actionMenu: actionMenu,
    submitButtonLabel: submitButtonLabel ?? null,
    additionalButtons: additionalButtons,
    tabs: tabs,
    fullPageForm: fullPageForm,
    mainAttributes: mainAttributes,
    mainFormAttributes: mainFormAttributes,
    formActions: formActions,
    saveShortcutRedirect: saveShortcutRedirect ?? null,
    contentNotice: contentNotice,
    bodyClass: bodyClass,
    elementIndex: elementIndex ?? null,
    content: content ~ footerHtml,
    details: details,
    sidebar: sidebar,
    errorSummary: errorSummary ?? null,
}) -%}
